From 1a97edd34f48c7dea2a9e7cb0e6b6d7c4f1a58d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:56:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the backfill the way Frappe can resolve it

bench migrate aborted:

    execute_patch -> exec(patch, globals())
    NameError: name 'murasalat_office' is not defined

patch_handler.execute_patch has two branches. A line prefixed with `execute:` is documented
there as being for "simple python commands" and is exec'd as raw Python in patch_handler's own
globals - which hold no app name, only what that module imported - so a third-party module
path cannot resolve. The other branch resolves the line with frappe.get_attr, which imports
the module properly. The backfill is therefore listed as a bare module path.

The two v0_2x lines keep their legacy text deliberately: the line itself is the key in the
Patch Log, so rewriting them would make Frappe treat them as new patches and run them again.

The patch function also gains a docstring, since Frappe prints it during migrate, and the test
that asserted the broken declaration now guards against its return.
